 "text": "The first week in a new job can feel strange. There are new names, new systems and new rules. Here is what helped me. On the first day, I wrote down the name of everyone I met. I asked my manager what success would look like after three months. That one question gave me a clear direction. I also found one colleague who was willing to answer small questions. I tried not to change things too quickly. Instead, I watched how the team worked and why. By the end of the first month, I felt at home. Every new job is a chance to learn, so give yourself time to settle."
